      "set_group": {
        "action": "set_group",
        "example": {
          "action": "set_group",
          "avID": "<avID>",
          "blockID": "<blockID>",
          "group": {
            "field": "<field>",
          },
          "viewID": "<viewID>",
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/av/set_group",
        "guidance": [
          "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
          "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically and materialize a SiYuan-style NodeAttributeView block in the target document through a transaction.",
          "Most follow-up AV reads and writes only need avID. MCP resolves the owning database block from row bindings, mirror database blocks, or the blocks-table AV block record; pass blockID when you need an exact database-block view context or fallback.",
          "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cells").",
          "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
          "av(action="set_column_options") replaces a select or multi-select key's complete option list. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict preflight; omitted options are intentionally removed. If SiYuan reports new names in append order, MCP returns that intermediate state and never sends a concealed reorder write.",
          "av(action="duplicate_rows") copies canonical, bound row item IDs into detached text records. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict manifest preflight; two-way relations also require rw/rwd permission on every resolved destination AV carrier. A lost response is never retried automatically.",
          "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; after materialization, MCP can usually rediscover that owning database block automatically.",
          "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
          "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
          "For add_view, set_filters, set_sorts, set_group, set_column_visibility, and set_column_order, always provide avID + blockID + viewID. blockID must be the exact NodeAttributeView carrier whose custom-sy-av-view currently equals viewID; MCP refuses kernel fallback.",
          "These view-configuration actions are strict writes: run the same action with validateOnly=true, then submit the returned requestId and returned expectedStateHash. Their persistence proof is raw getAttributeView plus carrier attrs/DOM, never renderAttributeView.",
          "set_filters and set_sorts replace their entire arrays; partial patch input is not supported. An empty filter list is persisted as the semantic empty AND root, even if Go omits its empty filters array on raw JSON readback.",
          "add_view creates only table, gallery, or kanban and names it in one native transaction. Kanban requires an existing select column so creation cannot silently synthesize a schema field in every existing view. The native transaction selects the new view on the supplied carrier and normalizes its visible-view list to the existing persisted view order plus that new ID; MCP verifies that exact effect. Use block(action="set_attrs") deliberately for any other visible-view curation.",
        ],
        "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + group. field="" clears grouping; numeric range method requires range. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Set or clear grouping on the exact view selected by a verified carrier.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "set_group",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "avID": {
              "description": "Attribute view ID",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "blockID": {
              "description": "Exact NodeAttributeView carrier block ID; kernel fallback is not permitted",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "group": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "field": {
                  "description": "Grouping key ID; empty string clears grouping",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "hideEmpty": {
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                "method": {
                  "description": "0=value, 1=numeric range, 2=relative date, 3=day, 4=week, 5=month, 6=year",
                  "maximum": 6,
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "type": "integer",
                },
                "order": {
                  "description": "0=ascending, 1=descending, 2=manual, 3=select-option order",
                  "maximum": 3,
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "type": "integer",
                },
                "range": {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "description": "Required by the kernel for numeric-range grouping",
                  "properties": {
                    "numEnd": {
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "numStart": {
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "numStep": {
                      "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "numStart",
                    "numEnd",
                    "numStep",
                  ],
                  "type": "object",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "field",
                "method",
                "order",
                "hideEmpty",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "viewID": {
              "description": "The exact view currently selected by blockID; MCP rejects kernel fallback.",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "avID",
            "blockID",
            "viewID",
            "group",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "avID",
          "blockID",
          "viewID",
          "group",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": false,
        "shapes": [
          "avID + blockID + viewID + group",
        ],
        "tool": "av",
      },
      "set_new_item_templates": {
        "action": "set_new_item_templates",
        "example": {
          "action": "set_new_item_templates",
          "avID": "<avID>",
          "blockID": "<blockID>",
          "defaultTemplateID": "<defaultTemplateID>",
          "templates": [
            {
              "id": "20240318112233-abc123",
            },
          ],
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/av/set_new_item_templates",
        "guidance": [
          "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
          "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically and materialize a SiYuan-style NodeAttributeView block in the target document through a transaction.",
          "Most follow-up AV reads and writes only need avID. MCP resolves the owning database block from row bindings, mirror database blocks, or the blocks-table AV block record; pass blockID when you need an exact database-block view context or fallback.",
          "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cells").",
          "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
          "av(action="set_column_options") replaces a select or multi-select key's complete option list. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict preflight; omitted options are intentionally removed. If SiYuan reports new names in append order, MCP returns that intermediate state and never sends a concealed reorder write.",
          "av(action="duplicate_rows") copies canonical, bound row item IDs into detached text records. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict manifest preflight; two-way relations also require rw/rwd permission on every resolved destination AV carrier. A lost response is never retried automatically.",
          "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; after materialization, MCP can usually rediscover that owning database block automatically.",
          "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
          "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
          "For add_view, set_filters, set_sorts, set_group, set_column_visibility, and set_column_order, always provide avID + blockID + viewID. blockID must be the exact NodeAttributeView carrier whose custom-sy-av-view currently equals viewID; MCP refuses kernel fallback.",
          "These view-configuration actions are strict writes: run the same action with validateOnly=true, then submit the returned requestId and returned expectedStateHash. Their persistence proof is raw getAttributeView plus carrier attrs/DOM, never renderAttributeView.",
          "set_filters and set_sorts replace their entire arrays; partial patch input is not supported. An empty filter list is persisted as the semantic empty AND root, even if Go omits its empty filters array on raw JSON readback.",
          "add_view creates only table, gallery, or kanban and names it in one native transaction. Kanban requires an existing select column so creation cannot silently synthesize a schema field in every existing view. The native transaction selects the new view on the supplied carrier and normalizes its visible-view list to the existing persisted view order plus that new ID; MCP verifies that exact effect. Use block(action="set_attrs") deliberately for any other visible-view curation.",
        ],
        "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of ordered native new-item templates. Pass every template and defaultTemplateID, not a patch. MCP captures a canonical complete-template preimage, validates each key and select/mSelect option against the raw AV, performs one native transaction, and verifies order, default, and all remaining template fields through getAttributeView. Missing options are rejected rather than added or silently pruned.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Replace the complete ordered native new-item-template configuration after checking each field against the current AV schema.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "set_new_item_templates",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "avID": {
              "description": "Attribute view ID",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "blockID": {
              "description": "Materialized database block used for permission and transaction context",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "defaultTemplateID": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                {
                  "const": "",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Default template ID, or empty to clear it; required because this replaces the complete configuration",
            },
            "templates": {
              "description": "Complete ordered replacement template array",
              "items": {
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "contentTemplatePath": {
                    "description": "Native content-template path for document targets",
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "fieldValues": {
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "additionalProperties": false,
                      "properties": {
                        "mode": {
                          "description": "Native new-item field-value mode",
                          "enum": [
                            "static",
                            "currentTime",
                          ],
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                        "value": {
                          "additionalProperties": {},
                          "description": "Native AV value payload; omitted for currentTime",
                          "type": "object",
                        },
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "mode",
                      ],
                      "type": "object",
                    },
                    "description": "Defaults keyed by AV key ID",
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "icon": {
                    "description": "Document template icon",
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "id": {
                    "description": "Stable new-item template ID",
                    "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "name": {
                    "description": "Template name; SiYuan trims surrounding whitespace",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "primaryKeyTemplate": {
                    "description": "Native Go-template primary-key source",
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "saveLocation": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "description": "Document target location; omitted means inherit SiYuan's document-create configuration",
                    "properties": {
                      "boxID": {
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "pathTemplate": {
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "pathTemplate",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "targetType": {
                    "description": "Whether creation makes a detached row or a document-bound row",
                    "enum": [
                      "detached",
                      "document",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                },
                "required": [
                  "id",
                  "name",
                  "targetType",
                ],
                "type": "object",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "avID",
            "blockID",
            "templates",
            "defaultTemplateID",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "avID",
          "blockID",
          "templates",
          "defaultTemplateID",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": true,
        "shapes": [
          "avID + blockID + templates + defaultTemplateID",
        ],
        "tool": "av",
      },
      "set_relation": {
        "action": "set_relation",
        "example": {
          "action": "set_relation",
          "avID": "<avID>",
          "blockID": "<blockID>",
          "itemID": "<itemID>",
          "keyID": "<keyID>",
          "relatedItemIDs": [
            "<relatedItemIDsItem>",
          ],
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/av/set_relation",
        "guidance": [
          "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
          "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically and materialize a SiYuan-style NodeAttributeView block in the target document through a transaction.",
          "Most follow-up AV reads and writes only need avID. MCP resolves the owning database block from row bindings, mirror database blocks, or the blocks-table AV block record; pass blockID when you need an exact database-block view context or fallback.",
          "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cells").",
          "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
          "av(action="set_column_options") replaces a select or multi-select key's complete option list. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict preflight; omitted options are intentionally removed. If SiYuan reports new names in append order, MCP returns that intermediate state and never sends a concealed reorder write.",
          "av(action="duplicate_rows") copies canonical, bound row item IDs into detached text records. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict manifest preflight; two-way relations also require rw/rwd permission on every resolved destination AV carrier. A lost response is never retried automatically.",
          "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; after materialization, MCP can usually rediscover that owning database block automatically.",
          "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
          "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
          "For add_view, set_filters, set_sorts, set_group, set_column_visibility, and set_column_order, always provide avID + blockID + viewID. blockID must be the exact NodeAttributeView carrier whose custom-sy-av-view currently equals viewID; MCP refuses kernel fallback.",
          "These view-configuration actions are strict writes: run the same action with validateOnly=true, then submit the returned requestId and returned expectedStateHash. Their persistence proof is raw getAttributeView plus carrier attrs/DOM, never renderAttributeView.",
          "set_filters and set_sorts replace their entire arrays; partial patch input is not supported. An empty filter list is persisted as the semantic empty AND root, even if Go omits its empty filters array on raw JSON readback.",
          "add_view creates only table, gallery, or kanban and names it in one native transaction. Kanban requires an existing select column so creation cannot silently synthesize a schema field in every existing view. The native transaction selects the new view on the supplied carrier and normalizes its visible-view list to the existing persisted view order plus that new ID; MCP verifies that exact effect. Use block(action="set_attrs") deliberately for any other visible-view curation.",
        ],
        "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of one relation cell. blockID is the verified source database carrier; itemID and relatedItemIDs are AV row item IDs, never bound document block IDs. An empty relatedItemIDs array clears the relation. MCP authorizes destination writes and verifies source plus two-way reverse cells without retrying an unknown response.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Set or clear one relation cell by AV item IDs, then verify the two-way reverse cell when configured.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "set_relation",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "avID": {
              "description": "Attribute view ID",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "blockID": {
              "description": "Verified source database block; relation writes never infer this from a row's bound block",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "itemID": {
              "description": "AV row item ID; never the bound document block ID",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "keyID": {
              "description": "Relation key ID",
              "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "relatedItemIDs": {
              "description": "Target AV row item IDs; an empty array clears the relation",
              "items": {
                "pattern": "^\\d{14}-[a-z0-9]{7}$",
                "type": "string",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "avID",
            "blockID",
            "itemID",
            "keyID",
            "relatedItemIDs",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "avID",
          "blockID",
          "itemID",
          "keyID",
          "relatedItemIDs",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": true,
        "shapes": [
          "avID + blockID + itemID + keyID + relatedItemIDs",
        ],
        "tool": "av",
      },
      "set_sorts": {
        "action": "set_sorts",
        "example": {
          "action": "set_sorts",
          "avID": "<avID>",
          "blockID": "<blockID>",
          "sorts": [
            {
              "column": "<column>",
            },
          ],
          "viewID": "<viewID>",
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/av/set_sorts",
        "guidance": [
          "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
          "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically and materialize a SiYuan-style NodeAttributeView block in the target document through a transaction.",
          "Most follow-up AV reads and writes only need avID. MCP resolves the owning database block from row bindings, mirror database blocks, or the blocks-table AV block record; pass blockID when you need an exact database-block view context or fallback.",
          "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cells").",
          "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
          "av(action="set_column_options") replaces a select or multi-select key's complete option list. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict preflight; omitted options are intentionally removed. If SiYuan reports new names in append order, MCP returns that intermediate state and never sends a concealed reorder write.",
          "av(action="duplicate_rows") copies canonical, bound row item IDs into detached text records. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict manifest preflight; two-way relations also require rw/rwd permission on every resolved destination AV carrier. A lost response is never retried automatically.",
          "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; after materialization, MCP can usually rediscover that owning database block automatically.",
          "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
          "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
          "For add_view, set_filters, set_sorts, set_group, set_column_visibility, and set_column_order, always provide avID + blockID + viewID. blockID must be the exact NodeAttributeView carrier whose custom-sy-av-view currently equals viewID; MCP refuses kernel fallback.",
          "These view-configuration actions are strict writes: run the same action with validateOnly=true, then submit the returned requestId and returned expectedStateHash. Their persistence proof is raw getAttributeView plus carrier attrs/DOM, never renderAttributeView.",
          "set_filters and set_sorts replace their entire arrays; partial patch input is not supported. An empty filter list is persisted as the semantic empty AND root, even if Go omits its empty filters array on raw JSON readback.",
          "add_view creates only table, gallery, or kanban and names it in one native transaction. Kanban requires an existing select column so creation cannot silently synthesize a schema field in every existing view. The native transaction selects the new view on the supplied carrier and normalizes its visible-view list to the existing persisted view order plus that new ID; MCP verifies that exact effect. Use block(action="set_attrs") deliberately for any other visible-view curation.",
        ],
        "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + the complete [{column, order}] array. [] clears all sorts; partial patch input is rejected by contract. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Replace the complete sort array on the exact view selected by a verified carrier.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "set_sorts",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "avID": {
              "description": "Attribute view ID",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "blockID": {
              "description": "Exact NodeAttributeView carrier block ID; kernel fallback is not permitted",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "sorts": {
              "description": "Complete replacement sort array; [] clears all sorts.",
              "items": {
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "column": {
                    "description": "Column key ID",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "order": {
                    "description": "Sort direction",
                    "enum": [
                      "ASC",
                      "DESC",
                    ],
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                },
                "required": [
                  "column",
                  "order",
                ],
                "type": "object",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
            "viewID": {
              "description": "The exact view currently selected by blockID; MCP rejects kernel fallback.",
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "avID",
            "blockID",
            "viewID",
            "sorts",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "avID",
          "blockID",
          "viewID",
          "sorts",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": false,
        "shapes": [
          "avID + blockID + viewID + sorts",
        ],
        "tool": "av",
      },
    },
    "description": "🗃️ Real databases: rows, columns, cells, views, filters, sorts, relations. Get avID from fs.read or av.search, then get for schema and resolvedRows before editing; use render for view rows. Reuse column IDs and resolvedRows.rowID; sourceBlockID and cell value IDs are different. Never edit database cells through fs/block. Read action help for nested writes.
Actions (required fields): get(avID) · render() · get_attribute_view_keys(avID) · get_attribute_view_filter_sort(avID) · search(keyword) · add_rows(avID) · remove_rows(avID, srcIDs) · add_column(avID, keyName, keyType) · remove_column(avID) · set_cells(avID) · set_column_options*(avID, keyID, options) · duplicate_rows*(avID, sourceRowIDs) · duplicate(avID) · get_primary_key_values(avID) · add_view(avID, blockID, viewID, layout, name) · set_filters(avID, blockID, viewID, filters) · set_sorts(avID, blockID, viewID, sorts) · set_group(avID, blockID, viewID, group) · set_column_visibility(avID, blockID, viewID, keyID, hidden) · set_column_order(avID, blockID, viewID, keyIDs) · set_new_item_templates*(avID, blockID, templates, defaultTemplateID) · create_from_template*(avID, blockID, templateID) · configure_two_way_relation*(avID, blockID, keyID, destinationAvID, backRelationKeyID, sourceName, destinationName) · configure_rollup*(avID, blockID, keyID, relationKeyID, destinationKeyID, calc) · set_relation*(avID, blockID, itemID, keyID, relatedItemIDs)
* = ask the user to confirm first. action="help" (topic=<action>) returns optional fields, nested shapes, and examples.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "add_column": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
        "add_rows": "Use avID + blockIDs to add existing blocks as bound rows, or avID + primaryKeyTexts to add detached rows whose primary key is plain text. Optional blockID/viewID/groupID/previousID refine the insertion target and preserve the intended database-block view/group defaults. MCP polls briefly after insertion and only reports success when each new row resolves to a writable rowID. To add initial non-primary-key cell values, follow add_rows with av(action="set_cells", avID, cells=[{rowID, columnID, valueType, ...}, ...]); reuse the rowID returned by add_rows.",
        "add_view": "Provide avID + exact NodeAttributeView blockID + a new stable viewID + table/gallery/kanban + name. First run validateOnly=true. It does not use render; kanban requires an existing select key to avoid an implicit schema write.",
        "configure_rollup": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing rollup key. Pass its existing relation key, destination key, and the native RollupCalc object exactly as SiYuan defines it. MCP does not invent calculation aliases. SiYuan may remove filters that reference the reconfigured rollup key.",
        "configure_two_way_relation": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing relation key. Pass source and destination AV identities plus a stable reverse-key ID. MCP verifies both writable database carriers, uses the native updateAttrViewColRelation transaction, and reads both directions back. It refuses to retarget an existing relation that would mutate an unpreflighted third AV.",
        "create_from_template": "Dangerous native creation using an existing template. itemID in the result is the AV row identity; blockID is the separate bound block/document identity. MCP preflights all default fields and relation targets, then reads every requested default back. Document templates require an explicit saveLocation so the target notebook can be authorized; inherited global document location is intentionally not guessed.",
        "duplicate": "Matches SiYuan copy-as-mirror behavior: call the kernel duplicate API, spin the AV block DOM, then commit an insert transaction. previousID overrides the insertion target; otherwise MCP uses blockID or the resolved owning database block.",
        "duplicate_rows": "Dangerous: use avID + ordered sourceRowIDs for bound, persistent top-level row items only; each becomes a detached text record. First call validateOnly=true, then confirm and submit expectedManifestHash + requestId. MCP checks every resolved two-way-relation destination AV carrier for rw/rwd before dispatch and verifies source placement plus reverse links after a normal response. Never retry automatically after outcome_unknown.",
        "get": "Call av(action="get", avID="<av-id>"); id is a deprecated alias. Returns the full AV payload after permission checks. blockID is optional and only needed for an exact database-block context or fallback permission resolution. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort": "Use avID + blockID to return the filters and sorts applied to that database block view.",
        "get_attribute_view_keys": "Use avID to return the database column definitions. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
        "get_primary_key_values": "Returns primary-key data in rows.key/rows.values and canonical IDs in resolvedRows. blockIDs are database carriers, not row IDs. Default pageSize is 16. Follow nextSteps for more rows; readInfo describes scope and permission filtering.",
        "remove_column": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
        "remove_rows": "Use avID + srcIDs to remove rows from the AV. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
        "render": "Use avID (id is a deprecated compatibility alias) plus optional blockID/viewID/page/pageSize/query to render database rows with the active view context. With createIfNotExist=true, blockID becomes the creation target; if avID is omitted, MCP generates one and materializes the database block automatically via a SiYuan-style transaction. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
        "search": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
        "set_cells": "Use avID + cells[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. For a single-cell write, pass rowID + columnID + valueType directly. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[]. Relation values are intentionally rejected here; use set_relation so MCP can authorize the destination AV and read back the reverse cell.",
        "set_column_options": "Dangerous: use avID + keyID + the complete options array for a select or mSelect key. This is a replacement, not a patch: omitted names are removed. First call the same action with validateOnly=true; after confirmation submit the returned expectedStateHash and the returned requestId. If new names are observed in SiYuan append order, MCP reports intermediate_option_order and requires a new preflight before any explicit reorder.",
        "set_column_order": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + every current keyID exactly once in desired order. Partial lists are refused. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "set_column_visibility": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + keyID + hidden. keyID must exist in that view layout. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "set_filters": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + the complete typed filter tree (at most 4 nested groups followed by a leaf). [] clears filters; raw readback accepts only the known empty AND-root normalization. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "set_group": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + group. field="" clears grouping; numeric range method requires range. First run validateOnly=true.",
        "set_new_item_templates": "Dangerous complete replacement of ordered native new-item templates. Pass every template and defaultTemplateID, not a patch. MCP captures a canonical complete-template preimage, validates each key and select/mSelect option against the raw AV, performs one native transaction, and verifies order, default, and all remaining template fields through getAttributeView. Missing options are rejected rather than added or silently pruned.",
        "set_relation": "Dangerous complete replacement of one relation cell. blockID is the verified source database carrier; itemID and relatedItemIDs are AV row item IDs, never bound document block IDs. An empty relatedItemIDs array clears the relation. MCP authorizes destination writes and verifies source plus two-way reverse cells without retrying an unknown response.",
        "set_sorts": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + the complete [{column, order}] array. [] clears all sorts; partial patch input is rejected by contract. First run validateOnly=true.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "add_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "add_rows": {
          "hint": "Use avID + blockIDs to add existing blocks as bound rows, or avID + primaryKeyTexts to add detached rows whose primary key is plain text. Optional blockID/viewID/groupID/previousID refine the insertion target and preserve the intended database-block view/group defaults. MCP polls briefly after insertion and only reports success when each new row resolves to a writable rowID. To add initial non-primary-key cell values, follow add_rows with av(action="set_cells", avID, cells=[{rowID, columnID, valueType, ...}, ...]); reuse the rowID returned by add_rows.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "add_view": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact NodeAttributeView blockID + a new stable viewID + table/gallery/kanban + name. First run validateOnly=true. It does not use render; kanban requires an existing select key to avoid an implicit schema write.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "configure_rollup": {
          "hint": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing rollup key. Pass its existing relation key, destination key, and the native RollupCalc object exactly as SiYuan defines it. MCP does not invent calculation aliases. SiYuan may remove filters that reference the reconfigured rollup key.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "configure_two_way_relation": {
          "hint": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing relation key. Pass source and destination AV identities plus a stable reverse-key ID. MCP verifies both writable database carriers, uses the native updateAttrViewColRelation transaction, and reads both directions back. It refuses to retarget an existing relation that would mutate an unpreflighted third AV.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "create_from_template": {
          "hint": "Dangerous native creation using an existing template. itemID in the result is the AV row identity; blockID is the separate bound block/document identity. MCP preflights all default fields and relation targets, then reads every requested default back. Document templates require an explicit saveLocation so the target notebook can be authorized; inherited global document location is intentionally not guessed.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "duplicate": {
          "hint": "Matches SiYuan copy-as-mirror behavior: call the kernel duplicate API, spin the AV block DOM, then commit an insert transaction. previousID overrides the insertion target; otherwise MCP uses blockID or the resolved owning database block.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "duplicate_rows": {
          "hint": "Dangerous: use avID + ordered sourceRowIDs for bound, persistent top-level row items only; each becomes a detached text record. First call validateOnly=true, then confirm and submit expectedManifestHash + requestId. MCP checks every resolved two-way-relation destination AV carrier for rw/rwd before dispatch and verifies source placement plus reverse links after a normal response. Never retry automatically after outcome_unknown.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "get": {
          "hint": "Call av(action="get", avID="<av-id>"); id is a deprecated alias. Returns the full AV payload after permission checks. blockID is optional and only needed for an exact database-block context or fallback permission resolution. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort": {
          "hint": "Use avID + blockID to return the filters and sorts applied to that database block view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_attribute_view_keys": {
          "hint": "Use avID to return the database column definitions. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_primary_key_values": {
          "hint": "Returns primary-key data in rows.key/rows.values and canonical IDs in resolvedRows. blockIDs are database carriers, not row IDs. Default pageSize is 16. Follow nextSteps for more rows; readInfo describes scope and permission filtering.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_rows": {
          "hint": "Use avID + srcIDs to remove rows from the AV. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "render": {
          "hint": "Use avID (id is a deprecated compatibility alias) plus optional blockID/viewID/page/pageSize/query to render database rows with the active view context. With createIfNotExist=true, blockID becomes the creation target; if avID is omitted, MCP generates one and materializes the database block automatically via a SiYuan-style transaction. readInfo distinguishes database/view scope and partial or unknown coverage. databaseContext identifies ID roles and existing field locations; nextSteps supplies enabled read/help calls. Never substitute sourceBlockID or a cell value ID for rowID.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "search": {
          "hint": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_cells": {
          "hint": "Use avID + cells[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. For a single-cell write, pass rowID + columnID + valueType directly. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[]. Relation values are intentionally rejected here; use set_relation so MCP can authorize the destination AV and read back the reverse cell.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_column_options": {
          "hint": "Dangerous: use avID + keyID + the complete options array for a select or mSelect key. This is a replacement, not a patch: omitted names are removed. First call the same action with validateOnly=true; after confirmation submit the returned expectedStateHash and the returned requestId. If new names are observed in SiYuan append order, MCP reports intermediate_option_order and requires a new preflight before any explicit reorder.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "set_column_order": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + every current keyID exactly once in desired order. Partial lists are refused. First run validateOnly=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_column_visibility": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + keyID + hidden. keyID must exist in that view layout. First run validateOnly=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_filters": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + the complete typed filter tree (at most 4 nested groups followed by a leaf). [] clears filters; raw readback accepts only the known empty AND-root normalization. First run validateOnly=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_group": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + group. field="" clears grouping; numeric range method requires range. First run validateOnly=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_new_item_templates": {
          "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of ordered native new-item templates. Pass every template and defaultTemplateID, not a patch. MCP captures a canonical complete-template preimage, validates each key and select/mSelect option against the raw AV, performs one native transaction, and verifies order, default, and all remaining template fields through getAttributeView. Missing options are rejected rather than added or silently pruned.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "set_relation": {
          "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of one relation cell. blockID is the verified source database carrier; itemID and relatedItemIDs are AV row item IDs, never bound document block IDs. An empty relatedItemIDs array clears the relation. MCP authorizes destination writes and verifies source plus two-way reverse cells without retrying an unknown response.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "set_sorts": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact carrier blockID + its current viewID + the complete [{column, order}] array. [] clears all sorts; partial patch input is rejected by contract. First run validateOnly=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
      },
      "advancedActions": [
        "add_rows",
        "remove_rows",
        "add_column",
        "remove_column",
        "set_cells",
        "set_column_options",
        "duplicate_rows",
        "duplicate",
        "add_view",
        "set_filters",
        "set_sorts",
        "set_group",
        "set_column_visibility",
        "set_column_order",
        "set_new_item_templates",
        "create_from_template",
        "configure_two_way_relation",
        "configure_rollup",
        "set_relation",
      ],
      "commonActions": [
        "get",
        "render",
        "get_attribute_view_keys",
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort",
        "search",
        "get_primary_key_values",
      ],
      "detailsHint": "Call av(action="help", topic="<actionName>") for required fields, shapes, and a minimal example.",
      "guidance": [
        "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
        "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically and materialize a SiYuan-style NodeAttributeView block in the target document through a transaction.",
        "Most follow-up AV reads and writes only need avID. MCP resolves the owning database block from row bindings, mirror database blocks, or the blocks-table AV block record; pass blockID when you need an exact database-block view context or fallback.",
        "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cells").",
        "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
        "av(action="set_column_options") replaces a select or multi-select key's complete option list. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict preflight; omitted options are intentionally removed. If SiYuan reports new names in append order, MCP returns that intermediate state and never sends a concealed reorder write.",
        "av(action="duplicate_rows") copies canonical, bound row item IDs into detached text records. It is dangerous and requires confirmation plus a strict manifest preflight; two-way relations also require rw/rwd permission on every resolved destination AV carrier. A lost response is never retried automatically.",
        "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; after materialization, MCP can usually rediscover that owning database block automatically.",
        "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
        "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
        "For add_view, set_filters, set_sorts, set_group, set_column_visibility, and set_column_order, always provide avID + blockID + viewID. blockID must be the exact NodeAttributeView carrier whose custom-sy-av-view currently equals viewID; MCP refuses kernel fallback.",
        "These view-configuration actions are strict writes: run the same action with validateOnly=true, then submit the returned requestId and returned expectedStateHash. Their persistence proof is raw getAttributeView plus carrier attrs/DOM, never renderAttributeView.",
        "set_filters and set_sorts replace their entire arrays; partial patch input is not supported. An empty filter list is persisted as the semantic empty AND root, even if Go omits its empty filters array on raw JSON readback.",
        "add_view creates only table, gallery, or kanban and names it in one native transaction. Kanban requires an existing select column so creation cannot silently synthesize a schema field in every existing view. The native transaction selects the new view on the supplied carrier and normalizes its visible-view list to the existing persisted view order plus that new ID; MCP verifies that exact effect. Use block(action="set_attrs") deliberately for any other visible-view curation.",
      ],
      "helpResources": [
        "siyuan://help/action/av/{action}",
        "siyuan://help/tool-overview",
        "siyuan://help/examples",
        "siyuan://help/ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "requiresConfirmation": [
        "set_column_options",
        "duplicate_rows",
        "set_new_item_templates",
        "create_from_template",
        "configure_two_way_relation",
        "configure_rollup",
        "set_relation",
      ],
      "sharedTopics": [
        "ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "tool": "av",
    },
  },
  "block": {
    "actions": {
      "add_to_daily_note": {
        "action": "add_to_daily_note",
        "example": {
          "action": "add_to_daily_note",
          "data": "- New item",
          "dataType": "markdown",
          "notebook": "20210808180117-czj9bvb",
          "position": "append",
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/block/add_to_daily_note",
        "guidance": [
          "block(action="prepend") or block(action="append") with a document ID targets the document start or end.",
          "block(action="update") is best for single-block replacement. One table, fenced code block, or list may contain many lines and still be one block. Use append/prepend/insert for multiple sibling blocks; verify the resulting structure after replacement.",
          "block(action="replace") only searches the kramdown of the single block identified by id. It does not traverse child blocks, sibling blocks, headings with their following content, or the whole document.",
          "Before block(action="replace"), call block(action="get_kramdown", id=...) and copy an exact old snippet from that result. It writes back through the original DOM text nodes; naked ((id)) references, footnotes, and siyuan://blocks links are allowed with backlink-semantics hints.",
          "block(action="prepend") or block(action="append") with a block ID targets that block's child list.",
          "To create real SiYuan tags inside markdown content, use the syntax #tag# with both leading and trailing # characters, then verify with tag(action="list", query="tag").",
          "To turn a block into a flashcard, prefer flashcard(action="create_card"). It writes "custom-riff-decks" and registers the riff card together.",
          "block(action="set_fold_state") requires a foldable block ID, not a document ID.",
          "block(action="recent_updated") is read-only; MCP filters unreadable notebooks first and then applies count.",
          "block(action="recent_updated") now presents the document-grouped summary as the primary user-facing view while keeping the raw block stream for advanced consumers.",
        ],
        "hint": "Use notebook + dataType + data + position ("append" or "prepend") to add content to today’s daily note.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Add a block to today's daily note, creating the note if needed.",
