          "file(action="read_template") reads Markdown template source through SiYuan’s authenticated /templates/ route; it does not expose arbitrary workspace files.",
          "file(action="create_template"|"update_template") writes Markdown templates through SiYuan’s /api/file/putFile workspace API; it does not write data/templates through the local filesystem.",
          "file(action="delete_template") removes an existing Markdown template resolved from SiYuan’s template picker and requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
          "file(action="save_doc_as_template") saves an existing document as a root-level template after read-permission checks; use create_template when you need a nested template path.",
          "file(action="render", engine="template") requires a template path inside the SiYuan workspace; arbitrary local paths like /tmp/... are rejected by the kernel.",
          "file(action="render", engine="template") uses SiYuan workspace template syntax .action{.title}, .action{.id}, .action{.name}, and .action{.alias}; it does not replace {{...}} placeholders.",
          "file(action="render", engine="sprig") uses inline Go/Sprig template syntax such as {{ now | date "2006-01-02" }}, but it has no document context.",
          "file(action="extract_doc") exports a document and all its assets into a self-contained uncompressed folder, so AI tools can read the files directly. Prefer this over export_resources when the goal is to inspect attachment content such as images, spreadsheets, or other binary files.",
          "file(action="audit_image_refs") compares caller-supplied expected image references with SiYuan's read-only direct image asset list. It uses multiset basename matching: every occurrence is preserved and matched once, including duplicate refs and different paths with the same basename. It ignores SiYuan timestamp/id filename suffixes, never reads local .sy files, and never repairs content.",
          "When Markdown contains an assets/... image and the task depends on its visual content, a vision-capable client should call file(action="read_image") for that one relevant image. Provide its path plus exactly one authorized document id or human-readable documentPath. Do not inline every document image automatically.",
          "file(action="get_image_ocr_text") reads OCR text already stored by SiYuan; it does not run OCR or cause SiYuan to generate OCR. Prefer read_image for direct visual understanding, and use stored OCR as a fallback for clients without vision support.",
        ],
        "hint": "Use assetsDirPath + exactly one of localFilePath or uploadSource. CLI/Node automatically stage local bytes when the kernel coordinator is enabled (10 MiB maximum); direct kernel clients POST {fileName,dataBase64} to the authenticated /plugin/private/siyuan-plugins-mcp-sisyphus/transfer/upload endpoint and use the returned uploadSource within 10 minutes. The file alias is accepted for localFilePath, and omitted assetsDirPath uses /assets/. This action reads the local filesystem and requires explicit user confirmation. Files larger than the configured large-upload threshold (10 MB by default) must be stopped, confirmed by the user, and retried with confirmLargeFile=true.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Upload a local file or a kernel-staged uploadSource to the specified assets directory.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "upload_asset",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "assetsDirPath": {
              "description": "Asset directory path (e.g., /assets/)",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "confirmLargeFile": {
              "description": "Set to true only after the user explicitly confirms uploading a file larger than the configured safety threshold.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "localFilePath": {
              "description": "Local file path. CLI/Node stage its bytes automatically when the kernel coordinator is enabled (maximum 10 MiB).",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "uploadSource": {
              "description": "Opaque source returned by the authenticated kernel /transfer/upload endpoint; expires after 10 minutes. Supply instead of localFilePath.",
              "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "assetsDirPath",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "assetsDirPath",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": true,
        "shapes": [
          "assetsDirPath",
        ],
        "tool": "file",
      },
    },
    "description": "📁 Assets, templates, and exports: upload/rename/delete assets, read images for vision (read_image), templates, Markdown/ZIP exports, unused-asset cleanup.
Actions (required fields): upload_asset*(assetsDirPath) · list_templates() · read_template(path) · create_template(path, markdown) · update_template(path, markdown) · delete_template*(path) · save_doc_as_template(id, name) · render(engine) · export_md(id) · export_markdown_snapshot(notebookID) · export_resources(paths) · list_unused_assets() · get_doc_assets(id) · audit_image_refs(id, expectedRefs) · read_image(path) · get_image_ocr_text() · remove_unused_assets*() · rename_asset(oldPath, newName) · delete_asset*(path) · extract_doc(id)
* = ask the user to confirm first. action="help" (topic=<action>) returns optional fields, nested shapes, and examples.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "audit_image_refs": "Use id + expectedRefs from source or preprocessed Markdown. The action reads only SiYuan's direct image asset references over HTTP and returns expectedRefs, actualRefs, missingRefs, extraRefs, counts, and ok. Matching is a multiset by basename: each occurrence is preserved and consumed once, so duplicates and same-basename paths are not silently merged. It ignores SiYuan timestamp/id suffixes; it does not read local files or repair imports.",
        "create_template": "Use path + markdown to create a Markdown template under data/templates. overwrite=false by default returns template_exists when the path already exists; pass overwrite=true to replace it.",
        "delete_asset": "requires: path",
        "delete_template": "Deletes an existing Markdown template after resolving it through SiYuan’s template picker. This action is dangerous and disabled by default.",
        "export_markdown_snapshot": "Provide notebookID plus exactly one of roots or documentIDs. Returns one deterministic, paginated page of Markdown with metadata/content hashes, path conflicts, errors, and an opaque cursor. It never writes the host filesystem and does not create a background job.",
        "export_md": "requires: id",
        "export_resources": "Provide one or more existing resource paths. Asset paths like assets/foo.txt are normalized to /data/assets/foo.txt before export. Set outputPath to also copy the exported ZIP to a local filesystem path. With the kernel coordinator enabled, CLI/Node request delivery=download and save the ZIP locally without overwriting existing files; direct kernel clients can use the returned downloadPath through the authenticated getFile API. Using outputPath is high-risk and requires explicit user confirmation. To extract attachments for direct reading without a ZIP archive, prefer extract_doc which produces an uncompressed folder.",
        "extract_doc": "Use a document ID + optional outputDir. Exports the document markdown and all referenced assets into an uncompressed folder, preserving original filenames. If outputDir is omitted, the default output root is ~/siyuan-extracted/; pass outputDir explicitly for a predictable path such as /private/tmp. With the kernel coordinator enabled, CLI/Node download the manifest into a fresh document directory, preserve existing siblings and reject an existing destination. Direct kernel clients can request delivery=download and save the returned Markdown and asset paths themselves. Without kernel delegation, the existing Node extraction behavior clears the entire output root first and skips unreadable assets. The returned extractedDir is an absolute path ready for direct file access.",
        "get_doc_assets": "Use a document ID to list assets directly referenced by the current document tree after read-permission checks. This does not expand query embed blocks; when the user needs to inspect the full document content and assets, guide them to file(action="extract_doc") instead. Use assetType="image" to return only direct image assets.",
        "get_image_ocr_text": "Use an asset path to read OCR text already stored by SiYuan. This action does not run OCR. Empty stored text returns available=false and points vision-capable clients to read_image.",
        "list_templates": "Searches SiYuan data/templates via the kernel template picker endpoint. Empty query lists all visible Markdown templates. Results include readArgs and renderArgsTemplate for reuse.",
        "list_unused_assets": "no extra fields",
        "read_image": "Use path plus exactly one of id or documentPath. MCP first authorizes that document tree and verifies that the image is directly referenced there, then returns metadata followed by one standard MCP image content block. Only PNG, JPEG, WebP, and GIF up to 20 MiB are accepted. It never writes a host file or runs OCR.",
        "read_template": "Use a path from list_templates, /data/templates/..., /templates/..., or a path relative to data/templates. Reads only Markdown template source and supports offset/limit pagination.",
        "remove_unused_assets": "no extra fields",
        "rename_asset": "requires: oldPath, newName",
        "render": "Use engine="template" with id + path for a workspace template; that engine uses .action{...} delimiters and exposes limited document fields such as id/title/name/alias. Set preview=true for SiYuan preview DOM. Use engine="sprig" with inline template for {{...}} syntax; Sprig has functions but no document context.",
        "save_doc_as_template": "Use id + name to save a document as a root-level template through SiYuan’s docSaveAsTemplate API. Slashes are rejected; pass overwrite=true to replace an existing root template.",
        "update_template": "Use path + markdown to replace an existing Markdown template. The template must resolve through list_templates first; otherwise MCP returns template_not_found.",
        "upload_asset": "Use assetsDirPath + exactly one of localFilePath or uploadSource. CLI/Node automatically stage local bytes when the kernel coordinator is enabled (10 MiB maximum); direct kernel clients POST {fileName,dataBase64} to the authenticated /plugin/private/siyuan-plugins-mcp-sisyphus/transfer/upload endpoint and use the returned uploadSource within 10 minutes. The file alias is accepted for localFilePath, and omitted assetsDirPath uses /assets/. This action reads the local filesystem and requires explicit user confirmation. Files larger than the configured large-upload threshold (10 MB by default) must be stopped, confirmed by the user, and retried with confirmLargeFile=true.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "audit_image_refs": {
          "hint": "Use id + expectedRefs from source or preprocessed Markdown. The action reads only SiYuan's direct image asset references over HTTP and returns expectedRefs, actualRefs, missingRefs, extraRefs, counts, and ok. Matching is a multiset by basename: each occurrence is preserved and consumed once, so duplicates and same-basename paths are not silently merged. It ignores SiYuan timestamp/id suffixes; it does not read local files or repair imports.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "create_template": {
          "hint": "Use path + markdown to create a Markdown template under data/templates. overwrite=false by default returns template_exists when the path already exists; pass overwrite=true to replace it.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "delete_asset": {
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "delete_template": {
          "hint": "Deletes an existing Markdown template after resolving it through SiYuan’s template picker. This action is dangerous and disabled by default.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "export_markdown_snapshot": {
          "hint": "Provide notebookID plus exactly one of roots or documentIDs. Returns one deterministic, paginated page of Markdown with metadata/content hashes, path conflicts, errors, and an opaque cursor. It never writes the host filesystem and does not create a background job.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "export_md": {
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "export_resources": {
          "hint": "Provide one or more existing resource paths. Asset paths like assets/foo.txt are normalized to /data/assets/foo.txt before export. Set outputPath to also copy the exported ZIP to a local filesystem path. With the kernel coordinator enabled, CLI/Node request delivery=download and save the ZIP locally without overwriting existing files; direct kernel clients can use the returned downloadPath through the authenticated getFile API. Using outputPath is high-risk and requires explicit user confirmation. To extract attachments for direct reading without a ZIP archive, prefer extract_doc which produces an uncompressed folder.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "extract_doc": {
          "hint": "Use a document ID + optional outputDir. Exports the document markdown and all referenced assets into an uncompressed folder, preserving original filenames. If outputDir is omitted, the default output root is ~/siyuan-extracted/; pass outputDir explicitly for a predictable path such as /private/tmp. With the kernel coordinator enabled, CLI/Node download the manifest into a fresh document directory, preserve existing siblings and reject an existing destination. Direct kernel clients can request delivery=download and save the returned Markdown and asset paths themselves. Without kernel delegation, the existing Node extraction behavior clears the entire output root first and skips unreadable assets. The returned extractedDir is an absolute path ready for direct file access.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_doc_assets": {
          "hint": "Use a document ID to list assets directly referenced by the current document tree after read-permission checks. This does not expand query embed blocks; when the user needs to inspect the full document content and assets, guide them to file(action="extract_doc") instead. Use assetType="image" to return only direct image assets.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_image_ocr_text": {
          "hint": "Use an asset path to read OCR text already stored by SiYuan. This action does not run OCR. Empty stored text returns available=false and points vision-capable clients to read_image.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "list_templates": {
          "hint": "Searches SiYuan data/templates via the kernel template picker endpoint. Empty query lists all visible Markdown templates. Results include readArgs and renderArgsTemplate for reuse.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "list_unused_assets": {
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "read_image": {
          "hint": "Use path plus exactly one of id or documentPath. MCP first authorizes that document tree and verifies that the image is directly referenced there, then returns metadata followed by one standard MCP image content block. Only PNG, JPEG, WebP, and GIF up to 20 MiB are accepted. It never writes a host file or runs OCR.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "read_template": {
          "hint": "Use a path from list_templates, /data/templates/..., /templates/..., or a path relative to data/templates. Reads only Markdown template source and supports offset/limit pagination.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_unused_assets": {
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "rename_asset": {
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "render": {
          "hint": "Use engine="template" with id + path for a workspace template; that engine uses .action{...} delimiters and exposes limited document fields such as id/title/name/alias. Set preview=true for SiYuan preview DOM. Use engine="sprig" with inline template for {{...}} syntax; Sprig has functions but no document context.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "save_doc_as_template": {
          "hint": "Use id + name to save a document as a root-level template through SiYuan’s docSaveAsTemplate API. Slashes are rejected; pass overwrite=true to replace an existing root template.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "update_template": {
          "hint": "Use path + markdown to replace an existing Markdown template. The template must resolve through list_templates first; otherwise MCP returns template_not_found.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "upload_asset": {
          "hint": "Use assetsDirPath + exactly one of localFilePath or uploadSource. CLI/Node automatically stage local bytes when the kernel coordinator is enabled (10 MiB maximum); direct kernel clients POST {fileName,dataBase64} to the authenticated /plugin/private/siyuan-plugins-mcp-sisyphus/transfer/upload endpoint and use the returned uploadSource within 10 minutes. The file alias is accepted for localFilePath, and omitted assetsDirPath uses /assets/. This action reads the local filesystem and requires explicit user confirmation. Files larger than the configured large-upload threshold (10 MB by default) must be stopped, confirmed by the user, and retried with confirmLargeFile=true.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
      },
      "advancedActions": [
        "delete_template",
        "render",
        "export_resources",
        "list_unused_assets",
        "get_image_ocr_text",
        "remove_unused_assets",
        "rename_asset",
        "delete_asset",
      ],
      "commonActions": [
        "upload_asset",
        "list_templates",
        "read_template",
        "create_template",
        "update_template",
        "save_doc_as_template",
        "export_md",
        "export_markdown_snapshot",
        "get_doc_assets",
        "audit_image_refs",
        "read_image",
        "extract_doc",
      ],
      "detailsHint": "Call file(action="help", topic="<actionName>") for required fields, shapes, and a minimal example.",
      "guidance": [
        "file(action="upload_asset") reads a local file path and uploads that file into SiYuan assets. Because it reads the local filesystem, it requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
        "If the file is larger than the configured large-upload threshold (10 MB by default), MCP must stop and ask the user for explicit confirmation before retrying with confirmLargeFile=true.",
        "file(action="export_resources") exports the given paths as a ZIP archive, normalizes common asset path formats, and can optionally save the ZIP to a local filesystem path.",
        "file(action="export_resources", outputPath=...) writes to the local filesystem and requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
        "Use file(action="list_templates") before rendering when you need to discover valid workspace template paths under data/templates.",
        "file(action="read_template") reads Markdown template source through SiYuan’s authenticated /templates/ route; it does not expose arbitrary workspace files.",
        "file(action="create_template"|"update_template") writes Markdown templates through SiYuan’s /api/file/putFile workspace API; it does not write data/templates through the local filesystem.",
        "file(action="delete_template") removes an existing Markdown template resolved from SiYuan’s template picker and requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
        "file(action="save_doc_as_template") saves an existing document as a root-level template after read-permission checks; use create_template when you need a nested template path.",
        "file(action="render", engine="template") requires a template path inside the SiYuan workspace; arbitrary local paths like /tmp/... are rejected by the kernel.",
        "file(action="render", engine="template") uses SiYuan workspace template syntax .action{.title}, .action{.id}, .action{.name}, and .action{.alias}; it does not replace {{...}} placeholders.",
        "file(action="render", engine="sprig") uses inline Go/Sprig template syntax such as {{ now | date "2006-01-02" }}, but it has no document context.",
        "file(action="extract_doc") exports a document and all its assets into a self-contained uncompressed folder, so AI tools can read the files directly. Prefer this over export_resources when the goal is to inspect attachment content such as images, spreadsheets, or other binary files.",
        "file(action="audit_image_refs") compares caller-supplied expected image references with SiYuan's read-only direct image asset list. It uses multiset basename matching: every occurrence is preserved and matched once, including duplicate refs and different paths with the same basename. It ignores SiYuan timestamp/id filename suffixes, never reads local .sy files, and never repairs content.",
        "When Markdown contains an assets/... image and the task depends on its visual content, a vision-capable client should call file(action="read_image") for that one relevant image. Provide its path plus exactly one authorized document id or human-readable documentPath. Do not inline every document image automatically.",
        "file(action="get_image_ocr_text") reads OCR text already stored by SiYuan; it does not run OCR or cause SiYuan to generate OCR. Prefer read_image for direct visual understanding, and use stored OCR as a fallback for clients without vision support.",
      ],
      "helpResources": [
        "siyuan://help/action/file/{action}",
        "siyuan://help/tool-overview",
        "siyuan://help/examples",
        "siyuan://help/ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "requiresConfirmation": [
        "upload_asset",
        "delete_template",
        "remove_unused_assets",
        "delete_asset",
      ],
      "sharedTopics": [
        "ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "tool": "file",
    },
  },
  "flashcard": {
    "actions": {
      "create_card": {
        "action": "create_card",
        "example": {
          "action": "create_card",
          "blockIDs": [
            "<blockIDsItem>",
          ],
          "deckID": "20230218211946-2kw8jgx",
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "description": "blockID is accepted as a convenience alias for blockIDs=[blockID].",
            "mcp": {
              "action": "create_card",
              "blockID": "20240318112233-abc123",
              "deckID": "20230218211946-2kw8jgx",
            },
            "title": "Create one flashcard from a content block",
          },
          {
            "mcp": {
              "action": "create_card",
              "blockIDs": [
                "20240318112233-abc123",
                "20240318112233-def456",
              ],
              "deckID": "20230218211946-2kw8jgx",
            },
            "title": "Create flashcards from multiple content blocks",
          },
        ],
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/flashcard/create_card",
        "guidance": [
          "flashcard actions cover review-first flashcard workflows and deck discovery.",
          "list_cards always reads from the kernel due-card endpoints and MCP post-filters cards by state for filter="new" or filter="old"; pass reviewedCards to match SiYuan's in-review filtering.",
          "get_cards returns all cards in a deck (not just due ones), with pagination. Use it to browse or audit deck contents.",
          "Prefer flashcard(action="create_card", deckID, blockIDs) when the goal is to turn existing blocks into real flashcards.",
          "create_card validates non-built-in deck IDs against get_decks, then calls SiYuan's riff add-card operation, which writes "custom-riff-decks" and registers the riff card transactionally.",
          "Create or locate the intended content block IDs first, then pass those IDs to create_card. Document block IDs are rejected; use content blocks such as headings or paragraphs.",
          "create_card(mode="attach") is retained for compatibility; SiYuan still writes the deck binding during the riff add-card operation. remove_card removes existing content block IDs such as paragraphs or headings from a deck; document blocks are rejected for creation.",
          "review_card requires a concrete deckID and cardID. Use list_cards or get_cards to resolve them; an empty deckID is not valid for review.",
          "Flashcard removal only removes riff card bindings from a deck. It does not delete the underlying note blocks; deleting note blocks is a separate block/document delete workflow.",
          "flashcard(action="remove_card") requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
        ],
        "hint": "Use deckID + content blockIDs to turn existing blocks into flashcards; single blockID is accepted as a convenience alias. Non-built-in deck IDs must already exist. Document block IDs are rejected. This calls SiYuan's addRiffCards flow, writes custom-riff-decks, verifies the binding, and creates deck records together.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Turn existing blocks into flashcards or attach existing blocks to a deck.",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "create_card",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "blockIDs": {
              "description": "Existing block IDs to turn into flashcards",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
              },
              "minItems": 1,
              "type": "array",
            },
            "deckID": {
              "description": "Deck ID",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "mode": {
              "description": "Compatibility option. SiYuan addRiffCards writes deck attrs and registers cards in both modes.",
              "enum": [
                "full",
                "attach",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "deckID",
            "blockIDs",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          "deckID",
          "blockIDs",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": false,
        "shapes": [
          "deckID + blockIDs",
        ],
        "tool": "flashcard",
      },
      "get_cards": {
        "action": "get_cards",
        "example": {
          "action": "get_cards",
          "deckID": "20230218211946-2kw8jgx",
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/flashcard/get_cards",
        "guidance": [
          "flashcard actions cover review-first flashcard workflows and deck discovery.",
          "list_cards always reads from the kernel due-card endpoints and MCP post-filters cards by state for filter="new" or filter="old"; pass reviewedCards to match SiYuan's in-review filtering.",
          "get_cards returns all cards in a deck (not just due ones), with pagination. Use it to browse or audit deck contents.",
          "Prefer flashcard(action="create_card", deckID, blockIDs) when the goal is to turn existing blocks into real flashcards.",
          "create_card validates non-built-in deck IDs against get_decks, then calls SiYuan's riff add-card operation, which writes "custom-riff-decks" and registers the riff card transactionally.",
          "Create or locate the intended content block IDs first, then pass those IDs to create_card. Document block IDs are rejected; use content blocks such as headings or paragraphs.",
          "create_card(mode="attach") is retained for compatibility; SiYuan still writes the deck binding during the riff add-card operation. remove_card removes existing content block IDs such as paragraphs or headings from a deck; document blocks are rejected for creation.",
          "review_card requires a concrete deckID and cardID. Use list_cards or get_cards to resolve them; an empty deckID is not valid for review.",
          "Flashcard removal only removes riff card bindings from a deck. It does not delete the underlying note blocks; deleting note blocks is a separate block/document delete workflow.",
